      "text": "First, we square the given equation to find $x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}$:\n\\[ \\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = 4^2 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 \\]\n\\[ x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 + 2 = 18 \\]\n\nNext, we square again to find $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}$. We multiply $x - \\frac{1}{x}$ by $x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}$ to get $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}$:\n\\[ \\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\right) = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\nSubstitute in the values we found:\n\\[ 4 \\cdot 18 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} = 72 \\]\n\nTherefore, \\(\\boxed{72}\\).",
